    <briefdescription>
<para>Libor forward model </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>References:</para><para>Stefan Weber, 2005, Efficient Calibration for <ref refid="class_quant_lib_1_1_libor" kindref="compound">Libor</ref> Market Models, (<ulink url="http://workshop.mathfinance.de/2005/papers/weber/slides.pdf">http://workshop.mathfinance.de/2005/papers/weber/slides.pdf</ulink>)</para><para>Damiano Brigo, Fabio Mercurio, Massimo Morini, 2003, Different Covariance Parameterizations of <ref refid="class_quant_lib_1_1_libor" kindref="compound">Libor</ref> Market Model and Joint Caps/Swaptions Calibration, (<ulink url="http://www.business.uts.edu.au/qfrc/conferences/qmf2001/Brigo_D.pdf">http://www.business.uts.edu.au/qfrc/conferences/qmf2001/Brigo_D.pdf</ulink></para><para><xrefsect id="test_1_test000026"><xreftitle>Tests</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>the correctness is tested using Monte-Carlo Simulation to reproduce swaption npvs, model calibration and exact cap pricing </para></xrefdescription></xrefsect></para>    </detaileddescription>
